  "evidence_notes": "Emma, 28, was diagnosed with Crohn's at 16. She has a history of multiple conventional therapies failing, including sulfasalazine, mesalamine, 6-MP, and methotrexate. She started Remicade, which worked for three years before she developed antibodies. She then switched to Humira, which worked for two years before losing effectiveness. She is currently on Stelara. She experiences injection anxiety, fatigue, joint pain, skin problems, and osteopenia. She also has anxiety disorder and PCOS. Her overall outcome is ongoing as she is managing her current treatment and its challenges."
